               <physDesc>
                  <typeDesc>
                     <p>Printed book.</p>
                  </typeDesc>
                  <bindingDesc>
                     <binding contemporary="true">
                        <p>Garrett Godfrey, rolls I and IV; it includes two fragments of early
                           13th-century Latin theological manuscripts, probably of English
                           origin.</p>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>
               <history>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName key="org_407" role="fmo">Norwich, Norfolk.
                        Dominican convent</orgName>
                     <p>Two imprints in one early binding, both with ownership note of frater Thomas
                        Bryggs, <q>Iste p<ex>er</ex>tinet ad ffr<ex>atrem</ex> Thom<ex>am</ex>
                           Bryggs <ex>con</ex>ue<ex>n</ex>t<ex>us</ex> ort
                           nortviciens<ex>is</ex></q>; part 1 has, in upper margin of A2r, <q>Liber
                           … ord<ex>in</ex>is p<ex>rae</ex>dica<ex>torum</ex> nortvic. ex dono
                              ff<ex>rat</ex>ris tho<ex>m</ex>e bryggs</q>. For Thomas Bryggs, ord.
                        subd. 22 September 1515, Cambridge convent, D.Th. Norwich convent, prior
                        1534, see A. B. Emden, <title>A survey of Dominicans in England</title>
                        (London, 1967), p. 289.</p></provenance>

                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">The volume was in the Sherbrooke sale, 27
                     June 1912, lot 458.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">First recorded in the Supplement to Medieval
                     Libraries of Great Britain (1987) with location untraced; it stated that part 2
                     was detached and appeared at Sotheby’s, London, 14 November 1918, lot 751 (sold
                     to Ellis). The <ref
                        target="https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990095411880203941/catalog">Harvard
                        Library catalogue</ref> states that the volume contains both
                     parts.</provenance>
               </history>
